# Playground flash / WIP assembly

When building or flashing `test/playground` (or any all-WIP integration build):

1. **Source of truth:** `docs/wip-app-ids.md`. Every claimed WIP ID (except upstream Sift **28**) must be in `faderpunk/src/apps/mod.rs` `register_apps!`.
2. **Never skip apps.** Current required WIP set: Heat Pump (29), Grooves (30), Golden Gate (31), Super LFO (32), Echolot (33), Arp de Levy (34), Chord Vamp (35), Hold Sam (36), **Harmonica (37)**, Loop de Cay (38), **Control Issues (39)**, **Venn (40)**, **Bassment (41)**, **Contura (42)**, **Manifold (43)**, **Giant Steps (44)**, **Axis Matrix (45)**. Update this list when `wip-app-ids.md` changes.
3. **Preflight on the ELF binary** with `rg -aF` (not UF2, not `strings` — UF2 splits payloads). `flash-now.sh` must abort unless each required CONFIG name is present. Keep that script in sync with the table. CONFIG strings (name, description, param names, enum variants) must be pure ASCII — `libfp` asserts it at compile time, so no `→`, `—`, `é` or `φ` in any `CONFIG`.
4. **ID 28 = Sift** — never register it. No need to leave a comment in `mod.rs`.
5. Before saying flash is done, confirm USB shows **Faderpunk** and note which WIP names were verified.
